WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.605 --> 00:00:11.608
Diego Alvarez: Hey Raj, hey Tanya. Like, How's Phoenix treating you? Still triple uh, digits down there?

2
00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:18.401
Raj Malhotra: Oh, we hit 102 yesterday. In October. My wife keeps asking why we don't move to Flagstaff.

3
00:00:19.313 --> 00:00:27.851
Tanya Mercer: And I've got two BDC reps out with the flu this week, so the phones have been chaos. But um, we're managing.

4
00:00:28.730 --> 00:00:38.825
Diego Alvarez: Oof. Uh, yeah, that's rough. Well, I know you both have a hard stop around five, so let me just say this is our renewal check in.

5
00:00:38.825 --> 00:00:46.303
Diego Alvarez: December first is the date. I want to hear what's working and what's not before we get into any paperwork.

6
00:00:47.255 --> 00:00:58.377
Raj Malhotra: Appreciate that. So, top line, the call tracking is doing what it's supposed to. We're tracking about 18,000 calls a month across the 22 rooftops now.

7
00:00:58.377 --> 00:01:04.366
Raj Malhotra: Google Ads and Meta are both feeding in, Salesforce is getting the BDC leads.

8
00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:08.096
Diego Alvarez: 18,000, that's up from what, 15 last quarter?

9
00:01:09.267 --> 00:01:17.717
Tanya Mercer: Yeah, we added the Henderson store in August, so that's part of it. Attribution looks right, the BDC team isn't complaining.

10
00:01:17.717 --> 00:01:24.960
Tanya Mercer: Signal AI is fine, the appointment booked signal is matching what we see in the CRM pretty closely.

11
00:01:25.277 --> 00:01:29.863
Diego Alvarez: Good, good. So what's on your mind for the the renewal?

12
00:01:30.117 --> 00:01:46.078
Raj Malhotra: Honestly? The money. Finance and procurement have been all over me. They look at the invoice and they see call tracking, and then they see Signal AI as a separate line, and then whatever else gets bolted on.

13
00:01:46.078 --> 00:01:54.058
Raj Malhotra: And they're asking why we're paying for things piece by piece instead of one you know, number per rooftop.

14
00:01:55.077 --> 00:02:05.506
Tanya Mercer: It's not just Raj's team. When procurement sees Signal AI priced as an add-on on top of call tracking, they start questioning the whole stack.

15
00:02:05.506 --> 00:02:15.100
Tanya Mercer: The way they see it, the platform should just include the intelligence part. They don't want to be nickel and dimed at renewal.

16
00:02:16.341 --> 00:02:25.907
Diego Alvarez: Okay, so, when you say add-ons, is it Signal AI specifically, like, or is it the way the whole bill is structured?

17
00:02:26.456 --> 00:02:36.596
Tanya Mercer: Both. But Signal AI is the one that gets circled. It's the line item they point at and say, why is this extra?

18
00:02:37.165 --> 00:02:52.228
Raj Malhotra: And I'll be straight with you, Diego. We've started taking calls from other vendors. Marchex has been in my inbox. Their per rooftop number comes in lower than what we're paying now, and procurement has seen that quote.

19
00:02:52.731 --> 00:02:58.608
Diego Alvarez: Got it. And is that a real evaluation or is it procurement doing their usual thing?

20
00:02:58.813 --> 00:03:12.698
Raj Malhotra: It's real enough so, that I have to bring them something. I'm not saying we're leaving, um, but the the like, renewal decision is tied to whether this add-on pricing friction gets resolved.

21
00:03:12.698 --> 00:03:14.381
Raj Malhotra: That's the honest answer.

22
00:03:15.433 --> 00:03:22.809
Diego Alvarez: I appreciate you saying that straight. Let me ask a couple things so I can take it back to my team properly.

23
00:03:22.809 --> 00:03:29.850
Diego Alvarez: When you say per rooftop, is Marchex quoting you the same 22 locations, or are they cherry picking the bigger stores?

24
00:03:30.259 --> 00:03:34.803
Raj Malhotra: All 22. Though I'd want to see the contract before I believed it.

25
00:03:35.835 --> 00:03:46.925
Diego Alvarez: Fair. And Tanya, on the Signal AI side, is the concern purely the line item, or is there something about how it's being used that's driving this?

26
00:03:47.988 --> 00:04:00.960
Tanya Mercer: No, usage is fine. It's purely how it shows up on the bill. If it were baked into the per rooftop rate, procurement wouldn't have a leg to stand on.

27
00:04:02.032 --> 00:04:12.209
Diego Alvarez: Okay. That's helpful. I don't want to promise anything on this call, because I can't restructure pricing by myself, but I can take the specific ask to my leadership.

28
00:04:12.209 --> 00:04:18.877
Diego Alvarez: What I'd want to bring them is: what would need to be true for you to sign in December?

29
00:04:19.756 --> 00:04:26.722
Raj Malhotra: A single per rooftop number that covers what we use, no separate add-on lines. That's the cleanest version.

30
00:04:28.102 --> 00:04:39.249
Tanya Mercer: And if there has to be a separate line, at least make it predictable. Right now every renewal it feels like something new gets added on.

31
00:04:40.347 --> 00:04:49.192
Diego Alvarez: Okay. Let me write that down exactly. One bundled per rooftop rate, or if not, no new add-on lines at renewal.

32
00:04:49.192 --> 00:04:53.404
Diego Alvarez: I'll get that in front of my director this week.

33
00:04:54.269 --> 00:05:03.282
Raj Malhotra: That works. And Diego, just so you know, I'm not trying to play hardball. I'd rather stay. The team knows the system.

34
00:05:04.380 --> 00:05:10.688
Diego Alvarez: I hear that that. And look, on the operational side, anything else I should know? Volumes, routing, anything weird?

35
00:05:10.982 --> 00:05:18.625
Tanya Mercer: Nothing weird. The Henderson store is still getting used to the call flow, but that's a training thing, um, not a platform thing.

36
00:05:18.625 --> 00:05:21.948
Tanya Mercer: We're doing a refresher with the the reps next Tuesday.

37
00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:26.313
Diego Alvarez: Okay, I can send you the flow diagram if that helps.

38
00:05:26.647 --> 00:05:32.167
Tanya Mercer: That would actually be great. Send it to my work email, not the BDC distro.

39
00:05:32.882 --> 00:05:40.212
Diego Alvarez: Will do. Alright, I'll let you both go. Raj, I'll follow up by Wednesday with whatever I hear. Tanya, diagram coming today.

40
00:05:41.642 --> 00:05:43.175
Raj Malhotra: Sounds good. Thanks Diego.

41
00:05:44.073 --> 00:05:47.231
Tanya Mercer: Thanks. And stay out of the sun this weekend.

42
00:05:48.093 --> 00:05:53.344
Diego Alvarez: Ha, I'm in Chicago, but I'll pass that along to my lawn. Talk soon.
